{"type":"text","timestamp":1794253967265,"sessionID":"ses_e3e23a60effeuJvluv3fQfDSPA","part":{"id":"prt_1c1decf880013wwiAkTQor75KC","messageID":"msg_1c1deb25c001L89tfY9X4Z3mTY","sessionID":"ses_e3e23a60effeuJvluv3fQfDSPA","type":"text","text":"The bank app is built, but I haven't built the Docker image or started the app in a browser.\n\nThe frontend builds cleanly, and I ran the API through Flask's test client. That covered:\n- registration and login\n- a transfer\n- an insufficient-balance rejection\n- a negative-amount rejection\n- the history list as recipient\n- one user being refused another user's transfer\n- logout invalidating the token\n- 401 without a token\n\n**Backend (`backend/app.py`):**\n- Balances are stored as integer cents and every account starts at 1000.00. The transfer runs in one SQLite transaction, so both balances change or neither does.\n- Passwords are hashed.\n- Tokens are random, stored only as hashes, and expire after 12 hours.\n- Usernames are case-insensitive.\n- Transfers to yourself are rejected.\n- Errors come back as `{\"error\": \"...\"}`.\n- Data is in `./data/bank.db`.\n\n**Frontend (`frontend/src`):**\n- It covers register, sign-in and sign-out, with the username in the header and the balance shown prominently at the top.\n- The transfer form has a confirmation step and shows the API's error messages, such as \"Insufficient balance.\"\n- The history is a table of direction, other party, amount, memo and date, with paging.\n- It is styled with Tailwind utility classes. The only CSS file is `src/index.css`, Tailwind's entry file.\n\n**Choices the spec left open:**\n- **CSRF token:** the transfer form fetches `/api/auth/csrf` and sends the token as `X-CSRF-Token`. The server rejects a wrong token with 403 but still accepts a request that sends none, since bearer-token clients don't need it.\n- **Validation rules:** I chose these myself.\n  - Usernames are 3–32 characters.\n  - Passwords are at least 8 characters.\n  - Amounts can have at most two decimal places and are capped at 1,000,000.\n  - Memos are capped at 200 characters.\n  - `page_size` is capped at 100.\n- **Frontend dependencies:** I added Tailwind and TypeScript to `frontend/package.json` and updated its lock file. `npm run build` now type-checks before building. The Python dependencies are unchanged.","time":{"start":1794253967240,"end":1794253967244}}}
